|      out[i] = clamp(v * factor, 0, 100)                                                         │      │▎ multiply, so a negative factor silently             │|
|    end                                                                                          │      │▎ maps every value to 0 instead of raising. Two       │|
|    return out                                                                                   │      │▎ options:                                            │|
|  end                                                                                            │      │▎                                                     │|
|                                                                                                 │      │▎ 1. Validate factor up front and error() on a        │|
|▌ function M.sum(values)                                                                         │      │▎    negative value.                                  │|
|    local total = 0                                                                              │      │▎ 2. Clamp the input first, then scale — this keeps   │|
|    for _, v in ipairs(values) do                                                                │      │▎    the contract but changes rounding.               │|
